+<!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="7a3a9225788080eb94f4df8c144c81b5a4154d5e1d96ded487393fb8c2a5e34c" reviewed-at="2026-11-08T00:00:00Z" -->
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Confirmed Ioniq 5 HDA2 applies CAMERA SCC=2, radar tracks=3, HDA2=1 and CustomSR=140, and turns Porter automatic SET, low-speed cancellation and dedicated GAP OFF. Returning to Porter restores the seven saved values. Other settings remain unchanged. Actual vehicle changes reset camera calibration and learned steering/control-delay values; same-car restarts retain them. Returning to a car starts calibration again rather than restoring its old values.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Enable with the current Porter configuration and restart on the Porter to save its baseline. Power down before moving the device and connect through the appropriate harness. Mid-drive toggle changes take effect at the next startup; OFF retains current values and uses manual car selection.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Only the observed Porter CAN signature and 2022–24 Ioniq 5 HDA2 are supported. Missing exact Ioniq ECU identification/HDA2 traffic or an incomplete Porter signature never falls back to the previous car for control. This feature does not resolve stock acceptance of automatic SET.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
+
